{
  "tool": "raster_grid",
  "owner": "FIT Stock Strategy",
  "version": "2026-10-17",
  "tolerance": {
    "rel": 1e-06,
    "abs_when_expected_zero": 1e-09,
    "note": "numbers relative 1e-6 (7 s.f.), zero compared abs 1e-9; integer outputs (T, counts, binary) exact; errors compared exactly as {error: schema class, reason: lower_snake_case code} (KAT_SCHEMA 17:46)"
  },
  "convention": "Images are row-major lists, row 0 at top, x to the right; at most 128 x 128, kernels odd and at most 5 x 5, at most 3 channels (scope cap). convolve is TRUE convolution (kernel rotated 180 deg, as in the textbook); modes: valid (only where the whole kernel fits, may be empty), same_zero (zero padding), same_replicate (edge pixels repeated). threshold: value >= T -> 1. otsu: 8-bit integer levels, class 0 = levels <= t, maximise between-class variance w0 w1 (mu0-mu1)^2, smallest t on ties; a one-level image reports T=0, variance 0. segment: connected components of non-zero pixels, 4- or 8-connectivity, areas sorted largest first. downsample: non-overlapping f x f block mean; output pixel size = input x f. channel_mix bt601: Y=0.299R+0.587G+0.114B. unmix: measured = M a for 2 channels, solved exactly; singular M -> MathError.",
  "oracle": "script-verified (textbook formulae); ChatGPT Chat cross-check pending. Expected values from plain-loop implementations of R. C. Gonzalez & R. E. Woods, Digital Image Processing (textbook); N. Otsu (1979), A threshold selection method from gray-level histograms, IEEE Trans. SMC 9:62; T. M. Lillesand et al., Remote Sensing and Image Interpretation (textbook); ITU-R BT.601 luma weights 0.299/0.587/0.114, https://www.itu.int/rec/R-REC-BT.601; T. Zimmermann et al. (2003), Spectral imaging and linear unmixing, FEBS Lett. 546:87; recomputed independently with scipy.signal.convolve2d, scipy.ndimage (convolve, label), numpy block reshaping, numpy.linalg.solve and a brute-force Otsu search over raw pixel lists",
